{
  "manufacturer": "Circutor",
  "model": "Computer SMART III",
  "short_model": "Computer SMART III",
  "aliases": [
    "Computer SMART III 6",
    "Computer SMART III 12",
    "SMART III"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power factor regulator with network analyzer)",
  "applies_to": "Circutor Computer SMART III reactive energy regulators (6 and 12 step models), RS-485 Modbus RTU, manual M015B01-03-25B.",
  "summary": "The Computer SMART III is Circutor's power factor (capacitor bank) regulator with a built-in three-phase network analyzer and an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Measurements are 32-bit integers in register pairs read with function 04. This map covers currents, reactive power split into consumed/generated and inductive/capacitive parts, apparent power, frequency, THD, energy counters and the quadrant sign registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "All addresses in the memory map are hexadecimal wire addresses; the manual's query example reads two registers from 0000 for L1 voltage."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Computer SMART III Instruction Manual",
    "doc_number": "M015B01-03-25B",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://docs.circutor.com/docs/M015B01-03.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 4.9, PDF pp. 59-70 (tables 13-15)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the manual's function 04 example returns 0000 then 084D (high word first), so 32-bit values are ABCD.",
    "Left out: all voltage registers. The table gives the unit as V/100 but the worked example decodes the same register as V x10 (212.5 V), so the scaling is contradictory.",
    "Left out: active power, signed reactive power, power factor and cos phi. The manual pairs PF/cos phi with separate kW/kvar sign registers but does not state the type or scaling of the PF values or whether the power values are signed.",
    "Left out: THD (unit printed as % with no scaling factor), temperature (signedness not stated), harmonics, relay/alarm/output words and the configuration registers.",
    "The kW/kvar sign registers are typed INT32 because the documented values are +1 and -1.",
    "Communication defaults come from the programming-variables table (Table 17): peripheral number 1, speed code 1 = 19200, parity 0 = none, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit. Frames longer than 80 bytes are rejected."
  ],
